The Fibonacci Tragedy.

Romeo, the first number.
Juliet, the second number.
Paris, the stored number.
Imogen, the input.
Lucio, the one.


Act I: The Fibonacci Calculation.

Scene I: Establishing the Characters.

[Enter Juliet and Lucio]

Juliet: Listen to your heart.

[Exit Juliet]
[Exit Lucio]
[Enter Imogen and Romeo]

Imogen: Thou art a pony.

[Exit Romeo]
[Enter Lucio]

Scene II: The Mathematics.

[Exit Lucio]
[Enter Juliet]

Imogen: Thou art as pretty as the sum of yourself and Romeo!

[Exit Juliet]
[Enter Romeo]

Imogen: Thou art as brave as the difference between Juliet and thyself!

[Exit Romeo]
[Enter Lucio]

Lucio: Thou art as pretty as the sum of thyself and a horse!

Imogen: Am I better than yourself?

Imogen: If not, let us proceed to scene II.

[Exeunt]

Scene III: The Output.

[Enter Imogen and Romeo]

Imogen: Open your heart!

[Exeunt]
